{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Unexpected closure — agreed\n\nD-055 · October 24, 2026.\nInterrupted active run = user Stop.\nRecover on reopening; show error popup.\n\n[[Unexpected Closure Recovery]]\n[[Run Lifecycle Design]]",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -450,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "reopen",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 1 · Granite reopens\n\nFind durable unfinished run/undo records.\nAn already-committed completed run stays completed.\nNo automatic restart of interrupted model work.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "fence",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 2 · Treat interruption as Stop\n\nInvalidate old approvals/callbacks.\nHold affected repository editing queues.\nDo not replay original tool actions.",
      "x": 540,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 400,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "popup",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 3 · Error popup\n\n“Granite closed unexpectedly. Interrupted work has been stopped.”\n\nShow recovery progress and update the result.\nOne popup can summarize affected chats.",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "settle",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 4 · Settle surviving writers\n\nApp closure does not prove every child process ended.\nCancel/settle harness-owned work.\nDetermine actual file/action outcomes before undo.",
      "x": 1640,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "restore",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 5 · Coding run: restore\n\nUse this run's durable undo record.\nPreserve pre-existing/newer user work.\nKeep earlier completed runs.\nNo model-generated undo or whole-tree Git reset.\n\n[[Run Lifecycle - Stop & Rollback.canvas]]",
      "x": 2200,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "verify",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 6 · Verify recovery\n\nReconcile partially finished restoration.\nSave the stopped outcome and actual restored state.\nAnother crash must not undo twice.",
      "x": 2780,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "done",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Restored and stopped\n\nPopup reports verified restoration.\nRetain conversation/history.\nRelease affected editing ownership.\nUser may start new work; no automatic continuation of the interrupted run.",
      "x": 3340,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "text_only",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Text / read-only interruption\n\nNo repository changes to restore.\nSettle and mark the run stopped.\nPopup reports the unexpected closure and interruption.",
      "x": 2200,
      "y": 520,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "attention",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Restoration needs attention\n\nPreserve current files and recovery data.\nIdentify conflicts/unknown effects.\nKeep repository editing blocked.\nPopup must not claim everything was restored.",
      "x": 3340,
      "y": 520,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "completed",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Completed earlier work stays\n\nA committed terminal success is not interrupted.\nDo not undo completed runs merely because the app later crashed.\nRestore only the interrupted run's tracked edits.",
      "x": 540,
      "y": 520,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "queued",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Queue / timer restart — agreed\n\nD-056.\nKeep pending messages; require explicit restart.\nFresh checks and queue positions.\n\n[[Restarted Queues & Timers]]",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 520,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "journal",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Durable undo before mutation\n\nRecord before/actual written state.\nKeep recovery data outside model-editable repository content.\nRecover without asking the model to reconstruct lost changes.",
      "x": 1640,
      "y": 520,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "restart_proposal",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Restart defaults — agreed\n\nD-056 · Accepted from P-014.\nThese extend the D-055 crash flow.\n\n[[Restarted Queues & Timers]]",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1020,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 300,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "pending_after_restart",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Queued messages remain\n\nShow “Not started — Granite restarted.”\nDo not dispatch automatically.\nUser runs pending messages explicitly.\nFresh validation, new run and queue position.",
      "x": 540,
      "y": 1020,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "held_timer_restart",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Previously held timer\n\nActive/queued temporary chat:\na fresh idle hour after recovery.\nRequeue → hold at 1:00:00 again.\nNo offline time deducted from a held timer.",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 1020,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "idle_timer_restart",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Already counting down\n\nExisting idle deadlines continue offline.\nAlready expired → normal cleanup.\nA restart does not revive the chat.\nOld approvals remain invalid.",
      "x": 1640,
      "y": 1020,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "recover_once",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Recover the transition once\n\nPersist recovered job/timer state.\nAnother restart must not recreate a job or repeatedly refresh expiry.\nDismissing the error popup starts no work.",
      "x": 2200,
      "y": 1020,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "6"
    }
  ],
